                <pb facs="0278" n="168" sameAs="frus:frus1931v03/pg168"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/2056: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-10-12T20:00:00+08:00">October 12, 1931—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 12—9:47 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>748. Your 388, October 11, 6 p.m. Since Hanson and Salisbury probably are en
                    route to Taonan, Colonel Margetts is being sent to Chinchow tonight, while
                    Lieutenant Brown will join him there from Mukden.</p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Engert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
